\chapter{UFSL–Continuity Co-Regulation}
\label{chap:coregulation}

\section{Overview}

UFSL–Continuity Co-Regulation is the bidirectional closed-loop mechanism that
binds latent-force dynamics to autopoietic identity preservation. While UFSL
integrates biological latent states, micro-environmental drivers, stochastic
noise, astrophysical entropy, and continuity constraints, the Continuity
Ontology ensures structural coherence, metabolic viability, and identity
preservation. Co-regulation ensures that these two layers stabilize each other
under multiscale forcing.

This chapter formalizes the co-regulation tensor, bidirectional modulation
rules, stability guarantees, and the closed-loop dynamics that ensure global
boundedness.

\section{Co-Regulation Tensor}

The co-regulation tensor $\Gamma(t)$ is defined as:
\[
\Gamma(t) =
\Theta(t) \otimes I(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\Theta(t)$ is the UFSL latent-force tensor,
    \item $I(t)$ is the continuity identity vector.
\end{itemize}

This tensor encodes:
\begin{itemize}
    \item identity-driven suppression of latent forces,
    \item latent-force-driven acceleration of autopoietic repair,
    \item multiscale stabilization,
    \item global boundedness.
\end{itemize}

\section{Identity-Driven UFSL Suppression}

Continuity identity suppresses UFSL forcing when degradation occurs:
\[
\Theta_{supp}(t) =
\Theta(t) \cdot
\exp\left(-\gamma \Delta I(t)\right),
\]
where:
\[
\Delta I(t) = \left|1 - \overline{I(t)}\right|.
\]

This ensures:
\begin{itemize}
    \item latent-force contraction decreases under identity threat,
    \item structural collapse is prevented,
    \item metabolic overload is suppressed,
    \item global stability is preserved.
\end{itemize}

\section{UFSL-Driven Continuity Acceleration}

UFSL accelerates continuity repair when identity is stable:
\[
I_{acc}(t) =
I(t) +
\lambda \cdot \|\Theta(t)\| \cdot I(t)\left(1 - I(t)\right),
\]
where $\lambda$ is a repair acceleration coefficient.

This mechanism:
\begin{itemize}
    \item enhances autopoietic repair,
    \item reinforces structural boundaries,
    \item stabilizes metabolic fluxes,
    \item increases resilience under perturbation.
\end{itemize}

